ld be B) False, because the premises directly lead to the mouse chasing itself. \n\nBut I\'m still torn because of the contradiction with premise 14. However, in logical reasoning tests, usually, you apply the rules as given without worrying about consistency between premises. So if the premises say that the mouse must chase itself (via 6,19,15), then the answer is B. \n\nTherefore, I think the intended answer is B) False.\n']  4%|▍         | 23/600 [43:04<21:41:07, 135.30s/it]
