['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is kind. Anne is red. Anne is round. Charlie is blue. Charlie is quiet. Charlie is red. Dave is blue. Erin is quiet. Erin is red. Erin is smart. If something is round then it is rough. Smart things are kind. If something is rough then it is kind. All blue things are red. Red things are round. All kind, blue things are round. If Dave is kind and Dave is rough then Dave is quiet.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Dave is not quiet.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:']
