['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nBob is white. Charlie is furry. Charlie is kind. Dave is cold. Dave is smart. Gary is red. Gary is white. Green, furry things are smart. If Charlie is white then Charlie is green. White things are kind. Cold, smart things are red. All furry things are cold. If Bob is kind and Bob is furry then Bob is smart. If something is cold and kind then it is white.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Charlie is smart.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:']
