['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nCharlie is nice. Charlie is quiet. Charlie is white. Charlie is young. Dave is not furry. Gary is quiet. Harry is furry. If something is nice and cold then it is quiet. If something is cold then it is young. Quiet, furry things are white. All furry things are cold. If something is young then it is nice.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Harry is round.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:']
