['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nCharlie is quiet. Dave is big. Dave is red. Dave is smart. Dave is young. Erin is big. Erin is blue. Erin is quiet. Erin is smart. Harry is big. Harry is furry. Harry is young. Blue people are red. If someone is quiet then they are big. If someone is furry then they are quiet. All quiet, big people are furry. If someone is young then they are blue. If someone is young then they are quiet. If Erin is furry then Erin is young. Blue people are quiet. If someone is furry then they are young.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Erin is not red.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:']
