were nice and young, he can\'t be round. \n\nWait, let me think again. Since Charlie is young (from smart → young), and Charlie is nice, then according to the contrapositive of statement 12, since he\'s young, he can\'t have both round and nice. But he is nice, so the only way to satisfy that is he can\'t be round. Because if he were round, then he would have both round and nice, which would violate the contrapositive (since he\'s young). \n\nTherefore, Charlie cannot be round. Therefore the statement "Charlie is round" would be false. \n\nLet me check if there\'s any other information that might contradict this. Let\'s see:\n\n- Charlie\'s attributes: furry, nice, smart, and therefore young. \n\n- Since he\'s young, he can\'t be both round and nice. Since he is nice, he must not be round. \n\nTherefore, Charlie is not round. So the answer should be B) False. \n\nWait, but let me check another angle. Is there any possibility that Charlie could be round despite that? Let\'s see: If Charlie were round, then since he is nice, the statement 12 would say he can\'t be young. But we already concluded Charlie is young (because smart → young). Therefore, that\'s a contradiction. Therefore, Charlie can\'t be round. \n\nSo the correct answer should be B) False.\n'] 43%|████▎     | 256/600 [7:05:44<8:58:10, 93.87s/it]  
