ary is big and quiet. The context doesn't say Gary is cold, so unless there's another rule that makes him cold. Let's see:\n\nGary is big, so he's smart (rule 8). So he's big and smart. Rule 7 says big, smart people are quiet. Well, Gary is already quiet, so that's consistent. But does he have any other attributes?\n\nNow, for rule 4: quiet and cold implies white. So if someone is both quiet and cold, then white. Let's see Gary: he's quiet but we don't know if he's cold. Unless there's a way he becomes cold. Alternatively, Fiona is cold, so if Fiona is quiet, but Fiona isn't stated to be quiet, so she can't be part of that. Harry is cold (from rule 6) and quiet? No, Harry is big, rough, smart, cold. Is Harry quiet? The context says Gary is quiet, not Harry. So Harry isn't quiet. So the only person who is both quiet and cold would be someone else. Wait, maybe Gary is not cold, so he can't trigger that. So maybe that rule doesn't apply to anyone yet.\n\nNow, let's look at rule 1: If someone is white and smart, then they are furry. Since all big people are smart (rule 8), so all big people are smart. So any big person is smart. So if a big person is also white, then they must be furry. But we need to see if any of them are white.\n\nRule 3: All furry people are white, so that's a one-way implication. But that doesn't help us unless someone is furry, then we know they are white.\n\nNow, let's see if we can find anyone's color (white) or if they are furry.\n\nLooking at Fiona: she is cold, rough, big, smart (since big). She's cold and quiet? No, she's not stated to be quiet. Wait, Fiona is cold and rough. Since she's rough, she's big and smart. But is she white? Let's see.\n\nIs there any rule that would make Fiona white? Let's see. The only rules that could imply someone is white are:\n\n- Rule 4: if quiet and cold \u2192 white. Fiona is cold but not quiet, so that doesn't apply.\n- Rule 3 says furry people are white, but unless Fiona is furry, which we don't know yet.\