y is cold. That\'s okay.\n\nAnother thing: the rule "All furry people are white" is mentioned twice, so that\'s just emphasis.\n\nRule 7: "Big, smart people are quiet." So anyone who is both big and smart must be quiet. Since all big people are smart (rule 8), so big people are smart, hence big and smart implies they are quiet. Therefore, all big people must be quiet? Wait, wait, rule 7 says "Big, smart people are quiet." Since all big people are smart (rule 8), then all big people are big and smart, so they must be quiet. Therefore, all big people are quiet?\n\nWait, that\'s a key point I might have missed earlier. Let me re-examine that.\n\nRule 8: If someone is big, then they are smart. So big → smart.\n\nRule 7: Big, smart people are quiet. So (big ∧ smart) → quiet.\n\nBut since all big people are smart (from rule 8), then for any big person, big ∧ smart is true, so they must be quiet. Therefore, every big person is quiet.\n\nWait, that\'s a crucial conclusion. So if someone is big, then they are smart (rule 8), and then since they are big and smart, they must be quiet (rule 7). Therefore, all big people are quiet. That\'s a big implication.\n\nTherefore, Gary, being big, must be quiet (which he is, as per the context). Harry, being big, must be quiet. So that\'s where Harry\'s quietness comes from. Similarly, Fiona, being big (since she\'s rough), must be quiet as well. Wait, Fiona is big because she\'s rough (rule 2). So Fiona is big → smart (rule 8), and then big and smart → quiet (rule 7). Therefore, Fiona must be quiet.\n\nBut in the context, Fiona\'s attributes are listed as cold and rough. But according to the rules, she must also be big, smart, and quiet. Therefore, Fiona is quiet. So now, Fiona is quiet and cold. Therefore, applying rule 4: if someone is quiet and cold → white. Since Fiona is both, she must be white. Therefore, Fiona is white.\n\nNow, Fiona is white and smart (because she\'s big → smart). So by rule 1, if someone is white and smart, they are furry. Therefore, Fiona must be furry. Since she\'s furry, by rule 3, she\'s white, which we already have.\n\nSo putting this all together:\n\nFiona\'s attributes:\n\n- rough (given)\n- cold (given)\n- big (because rough)\n- smart (because big)\n- quiet (because big and smart)\n- white (because quiet and cold)\n- furry (because white and smart)\n\nSo all that comes from the rules and the initial facts.\n\nNow, the original question is whether Fiona is not rough. The context explicitly states Fiona is rough, and none of the rules contradict that. In fact, the rules reinforce that being rough makes her big, etc., but don\'t negate her being rough.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Fiona is not rough" is false. So the answer should be B) False.\n\nWait, but let me check again because I might have missed something. The user\'s question is whether Fiona is *not* rough. Since the context says she is rough, unless there\'s a rule that says rough people can\'t be something else they are, but there isn\'t. For example, being furry requires being white and smart, which Fiona is, but that doesn\'t conflict with being rough. So no contradiction.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be B) False because Fiona is indeed rough, so the statement is false.\n'] 45%|████▌     | 271/600 [7:31:55<12:19:18, 134.83s/it]
