at's the key. \n\nTherefore, the conclusion is Fiona is kind, so the statement \"Fiona is not kind\" is false. The correct answer should be B) False.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe correct option is: B\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nReasoning:\n1. Fiona is big (given in the context).\n2. From the statement \"All big things are round\" (statement 16), Fiona must be round.\n3. From the statement \"If something is round then it is kind\" (statement 17), Fiona must be kind.\n4. Therefore, Fiona is kind, which directly contradicts the statement \"Fiona is not kind.\"\n5. No other rules or statements provide conflicting information that would negate Fiona being kind.\n\nThus, the statement \"Fiona is not kind\" is false. The correct answer is B.",
