['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nBob is nice. Bob is round. Bob is young. Dave is round. Erin is big. Erin is red. Gary is young. All round things are nice. All nice, big things are white. If something is big and white then it is round. Young things are nice. Big, red things are young. All nice things are quiet. All quiet things are big. Young, quiet things are red.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:']
