ing proceeds as follows:\n\n1. **Lion Eats the Cat**: \n   - The lion is green (given) and nice (given). \n   - Since the lion is nice, by the rule \"If something is nice then it sees the lion,\" the lion must see itself. \n   - Seeing the lion means (via \"If something sees the lion then it needs the dog\") the lion needs the dog. \n   - The lion is green and needs the dog, so by \"If something is green and needs the dog then it eats the cat,\" the lion must eat the cat.\n\n2. **Cat Needs the Bald Eagle**: \n   - The lion eats the cat and is green, so by \"If something is green and eats the cat then the cat needs the bald eagle,\" the cat must need the bald eagle.\n\n3. **Conclusion**: \n   - Since the cat needs the bald eagle, the statement \"The cat does not need the bald eagle\" is **false**.\n\nThe correct option is: B",
