ther angle: Let\'s see if any of the premises could lead us to conclude that Charlie is not white. For example, if there was a rule that says something like "if young and quiet, then not white," but there\'s no such rule. The only white-related rule is premise 10: quiet and furry → white. Since Charlie\'s furrieness is unknown, but his whiteness is stated, there\'s no conflict. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be B) False because the context explicitly states Charlie is white. The other premises don\'t contradict that, so the statement "Charlie is not white" is false.\n'] 53%|█████▎    | 320/600 [8:53:17<6:44:01, 86.58s/it] 
