['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nCharlie is young. Erin is blue. Erin is green. Fiona is big. Fiona is green. Gary is blue. Gary is green. All red things are furry. All furry things are red. Young things are red. If something is smart and not red then it is not green. All furry things are green. If something is red and green then it is blue. If something is young and big then it is smart. If something is blue and green then it is smart. Blue, red things are smart.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Charlie is smart.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:']
