is through being explicitly stated (cat) or via statement17, which the bald eagle doesn\'t satisfy, then the bald eagle cannot be round. Therefore, the statement "The bald eagle is round" is false, so answer B.\n\nWait, but if there\'s no rule that says only the cat is round, maybe there are other entities that could be round. For example, could the squirrel be round?\n\nThe squirrel\'s properties: cold and kind. To be round, it would need to satisfy statement17: if it chases the cat and is kind. But the squirrel doesn\'t chase the cat (it chases the bald eagle and lion), so it can\'t be round via that. So squirrel isn\'t round. The lion? There\'s no mention of it being round. The bald eagle? Only if there\'s another way, but there isn\'t. Therefore, the bald eagle is not round. Hence, the answer is B) False.\n'] 67%|██████▋   | 404/600 [11:22:18<7:25:52, 136.49s/it]
