['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nCharlie is big. Charlie is kind. Charlie is nice. Charlie is round. Erin is round. Fiona is cold. Fiona is kind. Fiona is round. Harry is round. Harry is smart. If something is blue then it is cold. Blue, cold things are nice. Blue things are big. All round things are blue. Smart things are blue. Round, smart things are kind. All nice, round things are smart. Nice, round things are big.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Erin is not smart.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:']
