['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is kind. Anne is young. Bob is rough. Charlie is cold. Charlie is kind. Charlie is rough. Charlie is smart. Fiona is kind. Fiona is rough. Fiona is smart. Rough, cold things are smart. All young things are kind. All kind things are blue. Young things are cold. If something is rough then it is cold. All young, blue things are kind. If something is cold and smart then it is young.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Bob is young.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:']
