he\'s green. So he could be furry or not.\n\nIf he is furry, then he must be kind → white → big. So in that case, he\'s white.\n\nIf he is not furry, then he can be white or not.\n\nTherefore, there are scenarios where he is white (if furry or not) and scenarios where he isn\'t (if not furry and not white). Therefore, since we can\'t determine it from the given info, the answer is unknown (C).\n\nWait, but let me check again the rules to ensure I didn\'t miss any.\n\nAnother rule: "If someone is white and not green then they are round." Since Dave is green, that doesn\'t affect him.\n\nWait, what about the rule "Furry, white people are rough." So if someone is both furry and white, they must be rough. But that doesn\'t impact Dave unless he is furry and white.\n\nHmm, I think I\'ve considered all the relevant rules. Since there\'s no contradiction in assuming Dave is white or not, the answer must be unknown. So the correct option is C.\n'] 70%|███████   | 421/600 [11:55:58<7:57:45, 160.14s/it]
