lie first. Charlie is round (from 1) and not young (from 2). Since Charlie is round, from rule 8, Charlie must be white. So Charlie is white.\n\nNow, from rule 14: if someone is white and round, then they are furry. Since Charlie is both white and round, this implies Charlie is furry. (Because white ∧ round → furry. So Charlie is furry.)\n\nNow, from rule 13: furry → rough. So Charlie being furry means Charlie must be rough. Wait, but is there any contradiction here?\n\nWait, but let\'s check if there\'s any other constraints. Let\'s see: Charlie is round, not young, white (from 8), furry (from 14), and therefore rough (from 13). So Charlie has the properties: round, ¬young, white, furry, rough.\n\nNow, let\'s see if Charlie can be cold or not. To check if Charlie is cold, we need to see if any rules prevent it or require it.\n\nLooking at the rules related to cold:\n\nRule 11: young ∧ big → ¬cold. But Charlie isn\'t young, so that doesn\'t apply.\n\nRule 12: round ∧ big → ¬cold. So if Charlie is round and big, then he can\'t be cold. Is Charlie big?\n\nTo determine if Charlie is big, we can check rule 10: round ∧ rough → big. Charlie is both round and rough (from above), so that means Charlie must be big. Therefore, Charlie is big.\n\nTherefore, since Charlie is round and big, rule 12 applies: round ∧ big → ¬cold. Therefore, Charlie cannot be cold. So the statement "Charlie is not cold" should be true. Therefore, the answer is A) True.\n\nWait a second, let me double-check if there\'s any other rule that could say something else about Charlie\'s coldness. For example, is there a rule that says something about furry people\'s coldness? Let\'s see:\n\nLooking through the list again, the only rules about cold are 11 and 12, and Erin being cold. Since Charlie is not young and is big and round, rule 12 applies. So yes, he must not be cold. So the answer is A.\n'] 77%|███████▋  | 462/600 [12:59:45<3:24:19, 88.83s/it] 
