l young people are furry*. Therefore, Erin must also be furry (though not explicitly stated in the context, this is a necessary inference).\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The statement \"Erin is not smart\" directly contradicts the conclusion that Erin is smart. Thus, the statement is **false**.\n\nThe correct option is: B",
