      "text": "\nOkay, let me try to work through this problem step by step. It's a logical reasoning question with a bunch of statements about different animals and their relationships. The question is whether the statement \"The rabbit does not visit the cow\" is true, false, or unknown. The options are A, B, or C.\n\nFirst, I need to parse all the given information carefully. Let me list out each of the statements one by one and see what they imply. Maybe I can make a table or some notes to keep track. \n\nStarting with the context:\n\n1. The bald eagle chases the lion.\n2. The bald eagle chases the rabbit.\n3. The bald eagle is big.\n4. The cow needs the bald eagle.\n5. The cow needs the rabbit.\n6. The lion chases the cow.\n7. The lion chases the rabbit.\n8. The lion is kind.\n9. The lion is not round.\n10. The lion needs the bald eagle.\n11. The lion does not visit the cow.\n12. The lion visits the rabbit.\n13. The rabbit chases the bald eagle.\n14. The rabbit visits the bald eagle.\n15. If someone needs the rabbit then the rabbit chases the lion. (Conditional)\n16. If someone is rough and they do not chase the rabbit then they visit the bald eagle. (Conditional)\n17. If someone chases the lion then they do not need the cow. (Conditional)\n18. If someone needs the bald eagle and the bald eagle chases the cow then the bald eagle is not round. (Conditional)\n19. If someone chases the bald eagle and they do not need the cow then they visit the cow. (Conditional)\n20. If someone needs the rabbit and the rabbit visits the cow then the rabbit is big. (Conditional)\n21. If someone is big then they do not visit the lion. (Conditional)\n\nThe question is about whether the rabbit does not visit the cow. So we need to determine if \"The rabbit does not visit the cow\" is true, false, or unknown based on the given info.\n\nLet me start by noting the existing statements about the rabbit's actions. From the given context:\n\n- The rabbit chases the bald eagle (statement 13)